                        "form": "opposabilités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e573786e-9ab4-3a54-8362-5af10fe80821",
                        "entry_id": "83a187e9-6a1f-3f50-9671-ce737ad09994",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualité de ce qui est opposable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65382c62-903f-427e-bf24-bb39751845e6",
                                "sense_id": "e573786e-9ab4-3a54-8362-5af10fe80821",
                                "text": "et que surtout chez les singes, l’opposabilité du pouce est toujours plus complète aux mains postérieures qu’aux antérieurs, ce qui est l’inverse chez l’homme."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e23b03d1-7876-3654-8e85-aea57812ca26",
                        "entry_id": "83a187e9-6a1f-3f50-9671-ce737ad09994",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère d’une situation juridique rendue obligatoire entre les différents acteurs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "989de75c-ad7d-4b59-8f97-e21fbf05a61b",
                                "sense_id": "e23b03d1-7876-3654-8e85-aea57812ca26",
                                "text": "L’opposabilité des actes n’est donc pas un vain mot, car, d’une part l’administration qui s’en prévaut est, en principe, légitimement fondée à le faire, d’autre part, les administrés, se voyant opposer ses actes, peuvent également en tirer bénéfice et s’en prévaloir contre leurs auteurs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95431693-b0db-49c9-9a47-26ea8a875644",
                        "source_entry_id": "83a187e9-6a1f-3f50-9671-ce737ad09994",
                        "target_lang_word": "opposability",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "opposability",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84336e2f-be8f-307a-8aac-26573fb6460c",
                                        "entry_id": "86a2fced-2864-30ae-b53c-57e2ffcfef6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition or quality of being opposable (capable of being placed opposite to something else)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "436d57ff-f291-4dbf-b9a5-8a40c7476506",
                                                "sense_id": "84336e2f-be8f-307a-8aac-26573fb6460c",
                                                "text": "Among the Primates themselves there is a whole group of living species, the South American marmosets, that, in the fore feet at least, show no evidence of opposability, although they are strictly arboreal in habits."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fde40e5a-1c6e-36c0-8129-9558d7e70e75",
                                        "entry_id": "86a2fced-2864-30ae-b53c-57e2ffcfef6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition or quality of being opposable (capable of being resisted)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "116ebcd0-ef74-495a-8f88-79adb47e0e1a",
                                                "sense_id": "fde40e5a-1c6e-36c0-8129-9558d7e70e75",
                                                "text": "This consequence remains hidden as long as custom is thought in terms of \"opposabilities\" in which the States' conduct is interpreted so as to render the same norm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a30136e5-856d-4302-8169-df0bffbbe9bd",
                                                "sense_id": "fde40e5a-1c6e-36c0-8129-9558d7e70e75",
                                                "text": "Although no provision of the Civil Code lays down the principle of invocability, it is nonetheless unanimously admitted and is found in substantive law in two forms: the opposability of the contract to third parties, and the opposability of the contract by third parties."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
